From 9df69ec83f86d81d406fe215fe179db3b585a3ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: test <test@local>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 11:42:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] P09.65d: end-to-end runtime wiring for cxx_throws Phase 1G
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Five fixes uncovered by a real-world smoke test that drove
an extern fn with #[rustc_cxx_throws] returning
Result<i32, CxxRawError> through the full compiler. Each
issue was a missing connection between the new
UnwindAction::CxxThrowsCleanup variant and existing MIR
infrastructure that had only ever needed to consider
UnwindAction::Cleanup.

1. mir/terminator.rs: successors() / successors_mut() only
   walked UnwindAction::Cleanup; CxxThrowsCleanup's bb was
   invisible to successor analysis, so downstream passes
   considered the err_wrap_bb unreachable and removed it,
   leading to "encountered jump to invalid bb" ICEs in the
   validator. Refactored both to use the new
   cleanup_block() / cleanup_block_mut() accessors. Made
   cleanup_block() pub.

2. mir/syntax.rs / mir/terminator.rs: added the matching
   cleanup_block_mut() accessor on UnwindAction so visitors
   that need to remap block indices can do so uniformly.

3. mir_transform/cxx_throws_wrap.rs: switched the err_wrap_bb
   from is_cleanup=true to is_cleanup=false. The catch
   terminates the unwind, so the err_wrap_bb is *not* part
   of the cleanup chain — it flows back into normal control
   on the assumption that the exception has been caught.

4. mir_transform/validate.rs: special-cased CxxThrowsCleanup
   edge-checking. Skip the standard
   "unwind edge target must be is_cleanup=true" rule and
   instead require the inverse — the target must be
   is_cleanup=false, since the catch terminates the unwind.
   This matches the semantics enforced by the codegen catch
   BB which lands the exception then re-enters normal code.

5. mir/visit.rs: super_terminator() for TerminatorKind::Call
   now visits the raw_err_local inside CxxThrowsCleanup so
   SimplifyLocals + LocalUpdater track use-counts and remap
   it correctly. Without this, raw_err_local's index went
   stale during SimplifyLocals + codegen indexed past the
   end of fx.locals.

6. mir/pretty.rs: fmt_successor_labels() now uses
   cleanup_block() to detect both Cleanup and
   CxxThrowsCleanup, so the successor-vs-label assertion
   stays consistent when dumping MIR (-Zdump-mir).

Verified end-to-end via:

    #[rustc_cxx_throws]
    fn maybe_throws(x: i32) -> Result<i32, CxxRawError>;
    match maybe_throws(x) { Ok(v) => v, Err(_) => -1 }

LLVM IR confirms:
- `invoke void @maybe_throws(...)` on call
- success → bb6 = Result::Ok wrap → match
- unwind → cxx_throws_catch → landingpad catch ptr null
- → __rustcc_cxx_catch_unknown(exn_ptr)
- → store helper result into raw_err_local slot
- → bb7 = Result::Err wrap → match

Phase 1 of v1.13.0 throws is now runtime-validated on the
Itanium codegen path (Linux + macOS). MSVC funclet path still
needs P09.66 — currently emits cleanup_pad + abort like
before this patch.
